# AdminKeyController — com.asrevo.cvhome.uaa.web.admin
#
# The signing keys: which one signs, which still verify, and "rotate now". No call here ever answers
# key material — the JWKS endpoint serves the public halves, and the private halves are encrypted at
# rest and never read back over HTTP. Addressed through store-core-gateway (`/uaa/**`).
#
# Behind SCOPE_super_admin / ROLE_SUPER_ADMIN. Requires a running stack: lcl start -d

### the posture — 200 KeyStatus {activeKid, activatedAt, rotationDays, nextRotationAt, retireDays, retiringCount, unusableCount}
GET {{SELLER_UI_URL}}/uaa/api/v1/admin/keys/status
Cookie: STORE-CORE-GATEWAY-JSESSIONID={{SUPER_ADMIN_SESSION_ID}}

### every key, newest first — 200 SigningKeyDto[] (kid, algorithm, status ACTIVE|RETIRING|RETIRED, the four instants)
GET {{SELLER_UI_URL}}/uaa/api/v1/admin/keys
Cookie: STORE-CORE-GATEWAY-JSESSIONID={{SUPER_ADMIN_SESSION_ID}}

### rotate now — 200 the new ACTIVE key; the previous one is RETIRING for settings.keys.retireDays
# Tokens signed by the previous key keep verifying until it retires. Resource servers that cache the
# JWKS refetch on the unknown kid the next token carries.
POST {{SELLER_UI_URL}}/uaa/api/v1/admin/keys/rotate
Cookie: STORE-CORE-GATEWAY-JSESSIONID={{SUPER_ADMIN_SESSION_ID}}

> {%
    client.test("rotated", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.status === "ACTIVE", "status " + response.body.status);
    });
%}

### the public halves, as every resource server reads them — 200, never a `d`, `p` or `q` member
GET {{UAA_URL}}/oauth2/jwks

### as a non-super-admin — 403
GET {{SELLER_UI_URL}}/uaa/api/v1/admin/keys
Cookie: STORE-CORE-GATEWAY-JSESSIONID={{ORG_ADMIN_SESSION_ID}}
